{"questions":[{"question_id":"lv5grwn0","content":"<p>Give below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R:</p>\n<p>Assertion A: The stability order of +1 oxidation state of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, In and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl.</p>\n<p>Reason R: The inert pair effect stabilizes the lower oxidation state down the group.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 8th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pgive-below-are-two-statements-one-is-labelled-as-asserti-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-5fhkbi0i9oiccwtw","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Give below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R:</p>\n<p>Assertion A: The stability order of +1 oxidation state of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, In and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl.</p>\n<p>Reason R: The inert pair effect stabilizes the lower oxidation state down the group.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A is true but R is false."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A."},{"identifier":"C","content":"A is false but R is true."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A."}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>To evaluate the statements provided, let's first understand the concepts involved:</p>\n\n<p><b>Assertion A:</b> The stability order of the +1 oxidation state of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, In, and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl.</p>\n\n<p><b>Reason R:</b> The inert pair effect stabilizes the lower oxidation state down the group.</p>\n\n<p>The elements <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Gallium), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Indium), and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Thallium) belong to Group 13 of the periodic table. As we move down this group, the +3 oxidation state becomes less stable while the +1 oxidation state becomes more stable. This trend is attributed to the inert pair effect.</p>\n\n<p>The inert pair effect refers to the reluctance of the s-electrons to participate in bonding as we move down the group in the periodic table. For Group 13 elements, this effect causes the lower +1 oxidation state to be more stable compared to the +3 oxidation state down the group.</p>\n\n<p>Given this, the Reason R correctly explains why the +1 oxidation state is more stable for <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> compared to <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, the stability order of the +1 oxidation state should indeed be Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl.</p>\n\n<p><b>Conclusion:</b> Both Assertion A and Reason R are true, and Reason R is the correct explanation for Assertion A.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is:</p>\n\n<p><b>Option D:</b> Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं। इनमें से एक को अभिकथन <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> एवं दूसरे को कारण <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.048ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.717ex\" height=\"1.593ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 759 704\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के रूप में दर्शाया गया है:</p>\n<p>अभिकथन A: <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.988ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2646.7 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1285,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1729.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> एवं <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.765ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 1222 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के +1 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था के स्थायित्व का क्रम है: <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.09ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.781ex\" height=\"1.686ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 6091.1 745\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1562.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2618.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3813.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4869.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(5591.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>कारण R: समूह में नीचे जाने पर अक्रिय युग्म प्रभाव निम्न ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था को स्थायित्व प्रदान करता है।</p>\n<p>उपर्युक्त कथनों के सन्दर्भ में नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर चुनें:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> सही है, परन्तु <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.665ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 736 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"52\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-52\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> गलत है"},{"identifier":"B","content":"दोनों कथन A एवं R सही है परन्तु R, कथन A की सही व्याख्या नहीं है"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A गलत है, परन्तु R सही है"},{"identifier":"D","content":"दोनों कथन A एवं R ��ही है तथा R, कथन A की सही व्याख्या है"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>प्रदान किए गए कथनों का मूल्यांकन करने के लिए, आइए पहले इसमें शामिल अवधारणाओं को समझें:</p>\n\n<p><b>कथन A:</b> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, In, और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> की +1 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था का स्थायित्व क्रम Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl है।</p>\n\n<p><b>कारण R:</b> अक्रिय युग्म प्रभाव समूह में नीचे जाने पर निम्न ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था को स्थायी बनाता है।</p>\n\n<p>तत्व <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (गैलियम), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (इंडियम), और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (थैलियम) आवर्त सारणी के समूह 13 से संबंधित हैं। जैसे-जैसे हम इस समूह में नीचे जाते हैं, +3 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था कम स्थिर हो जाती है जबकि +1 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था अधिक स्थिर हो जाती है। यह प्रवृत्ति अक्रिय युग्म प्रभाव के लिए जिम्मेदार है।</p>\n\n<p>अक्रिय युग्म प्रभाव आवर्त सारणी में समूह में नीचे जाने पर s-इलेक्ट्रॉनों की बंधन में भाग लेने की अनिच्छा को संदर्भित करता है। समूह 13 तत्वों के लिए, यह प्रभाव समूह में नीचे जाने पर निम्न +1 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था को +3 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था की तुलना में अधिक स्थिर बनाता है।</p>\n\n<p>इसे देखते हुए, कारण R सही ढंग से बताता है कि <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> की तुलना में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के लिए +1 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था अधिक स्थिर क्यों है। इसलिए, +1 ऑक्सीकरण अवस्था का स्थायित्व क्रम वास्तव में Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl होना चाहिए।</p>\n\n<p><b>निष्कर्ष:</b> कथन A और कारण R दोनों सत्य हैं, और कारण R, कथन A के लिए सही स्पष्टीकरण है।</p>\n\n<p>इसलिए, सही उत्तर है:</p>\n\n<p><b>विकल्प D:</b> A और R दोनों सत्य हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या है।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"group-13-elements-boron-family","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A is true but R is false."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A."},{"identifier":"C","content":"A is false but R is true."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A."}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>To evaluate the statements provided, let's first understand the concepts involved:</p>\n\n<p><b>Assertion A:</b> The stability order of the +1 oxidation state of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, In, and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl.</p>\n\n<p><b>Reason R:</b> The inert pair effect stabilizes the lower oxidation state down the group.</p>\n\n<p>The elements <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Gallium), <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Indium), and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Thallium) belong to Group 13 of the periodic table. As we move down this group, the +3 oxidation state becomes less stable while the +1 oxidation state becomes more stable. This trend is attributed to the inert pair effect.</p>\n\n<p>The inert pair effect refers to the reluctance of the s-electrons to participate in bonding as we move down the group in the periodic table. For Group 13 elements, this effect causes the lower +1 oxidation state to be more stable compared to the +3 oxidation state down the group.</p>\n\n<p>Given this, the Reason R correctly explains why the +1 oxidation state is more stable for <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1000 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> compared to <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.907ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1285 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"47\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-47\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(785,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.075ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 917 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(361,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, the stability order of the +1 oxidation state should indeed be Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl.</p>\n\n<p><b>Conclusion:</b> Both Assertion A and Reason R are true, and Reason R is the correct explanation for Assertion A.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is:</p>\n\n<p><b>Option D:</b> Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.</p>"}]}